## RFCs (`docs/rfc/`)

Feature **specs** — numbered RFCs, not semver files.

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[planned]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

| Body status | Filename tag | Location |
|-------------|--------------|----------|
| `draft` | `[draft]` | Spec exists; not scheduled |
| `planned` | `[planned]` | You explicitly scheduled it |
| `open` | `[open]` | Actively in progress |
| `partial` / `stub` | `[partial]` | Code started, not shippable |
| `fixed` | `[fixed]` | `docs/rfc/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `[canceled]` | `docs/rfc/canceled/` — will not build |

### Mandatory RFC body sections

Every RFC body includes (in this order, after the `#` title):

1. **Metadata block** — `**Version:**`, `**Status:**` (required); optional `**Target version:**`, `**Depends on:**`, `**Area:**` (key paths)
2. **`## Status at a glance`** — same pattern as [migration phases](../../docs/migration/fixed/02-[fixed]-rust-engine-complete.md#status-at-a-glance):

```markdown
## Status at a glance

| | |
|--|--|
| **Progress** | **4 / 6** components · **0 / 4** acceptance (v1.1 slice) |
| **Current slice** | v1.1 — wire overlay + server grid |
| **Backlog** | [1.0.0](../backlog/1.0.0-[draft].md) |
```

3. **`## Summary`** — then existing Components / Acceptance / Related sections unchanged

**Progress rules** (derived from existing tables/checkboxes — no duplicate task lists):

- **Components table:** count `Shipped` rows / total rows
- **Acceptance checkboxes:** count `[x]` / total for the **current target slice** (highest incomplete `## Acceptance (vX.Y)` or slice named in active backlog)
- Shipped earlier slices: second metric OK — e.g. `3 / 3 acceptance (v1.0) · 0 / 3 (v1.1)`
- **`[fixed]`:** `**Progress** | **Complete**` (+ final acceptance counts if useful)
- **`[draft]` / stub-only:** `0 / N acceptance (spec)` or `Spec only — not scheduled`
- **Meta/bundle RFCs** (012, 013): progress from meta acceptance checklist or child RFC links — no third task system

When a slice ships or component status changes: update glance **and** [RFC README](../../docs/rfc/README.md) **Progress** column in the **same turn** as checkbox/table edits.

